                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba2f9d7e-216e-3821-9e65-e7041fcb5ef4",
                        "entry_id": "13e84e3e-94f8-3e1f-a7e6-88d3ed9a71c2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "endearing diminutive of бара́н (barán): little sheep, little ram, lamb"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "diminutive",
                            "endearing",
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "92f08d36-6af4-4c40-94b4-3d9564d1de31",
                                "sense_id": "ba2f9d7e-216e-3821-9e65-e7041fcb5ef4",
                                "text": "Вошё́л с ра́достным гро́мким сме́хом Па́вел Васи́льевич Воло́дин, молодо́й челове́к, весь, и лицо́м, и ухва́тками, удиви́тельно похо́жий на бара́шка: во́лосы, как у бара́шка, курча́вые, глаза́ вы́пуклые и тупы́е, — всё как у весё́лого бара́шка, — глу́пый молодо́й челове́к.",
                                "translation": "Pavel Vassilyevitch Volodin entered with a loud, gay laugh. He was a young man who, face, manners and all, strangely resembled a young ram; his hair, like a ram's, was curly; his eyes, protruding and dull; everything about him, in fact, suggested a lively ram—a stupid young man.",
                                "english": "Pavel Vassilyevitch Volodin entered with a loud, gay laugh. He was a young man who, face, manners and all, strangely resembled a young ram; his hair, like a ram's, was curly; his eyes, protruding and dull; everything about him, in fact, suggested a lively ram—a stupid young man."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
